A Widget is the basic building block of a Flutter UI.

Things you see in a Flutter app are represented using widgets:

Text
Button
Image
Container
Row
Column
Scaffold
AppBar

Even things that don't directly appear visually, such as layout or behavior-related structures, are represented through widgets.


For example:

Column(
  children: [
    Text('Hello'),
    ElevatedButton(
      onPressed: () {},
      child: Text('Click'),
    ),
  ],
)

Here:

Column → Widget
Text → Widget
ElevatedButton → Widget
Text inside the button → Widget
Important interview concept

Flutter UI is basically a tree of widgets.

For example:

MaterialApp
   ↓
Scaffold
   ↓
Column
   ├── Text
   └── ElevatedButton
          ↓
        Text

This is called the Widget Tree.